// --- display ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// HS20HS072RX, 240x320, ST7789 (read back as ID 0x858552), 4-wire SPI on FPC P2: pins 1 GND, 2 CS,
// 3 RS (D/C), 4 SCL, 5 SDA, 6 RST, 7 NC, 8 IOVCC, 9 VCC, 10 LED-A, 11 LED-K, 12 GND (eBadge
// display.kicad_sch; netlist P2 pins 2-6 = GPIO0, 45, 46, 3, 1; this pin map is the one asm_13 draws
// through). SDA is bidirectional: the controller answers reads on it. The sheet's "SPI CS: 10" is
// wrong. RST has a 100 k pull-down (R39, "Default: Reset State"): the panel stays in reset until
// GPIO1 is driven high. Driven bit-banged by asm_13 (SPI2 itself is unused so far, window index 9).
//
// Two rules the panel enforced, both found by reading its status back (2026-09-29):
//   - every command byte starts its own chip-select transaction (CS high, ~5 us, CS low): after
//     SWRESET nothing is accepted until CS has deasserted; parameters and pixel data stay in the
//     command's transaction;
//   - clock edges issued back to back from the write buffer (~25 ns apart at 40 MHz) and 5-cycle
//     nop-timed pulses (~125 ns) were ignored; edges each performed by a memw, one call per clock
//     (roughly 0.5 us half-periods at 40 MHz), are accepted.
// Inversion (INVON) is needed or 0xFFFF shows black. MADCTL 0xA0 gives landscape with the flex on
// the left and text upright (320 columns x 240 rows). Register reads: 24/32-bit ones (RDDID,
// RDDST) need one dummy clock, 8-bit ones (RDDPM, RDDCOLMOD, RDDMADCTL) none, RAMRD one dummy byte
// then 3 bytes per pixel. The backlight is not switchable: +3.3 V through R18 (100 ohm) into LED-A,
// four white LEDs in parallel rated 80 mA, so it runs at a few milliamps and is dim in room light.

fn pin_display_cs() -> int64 {
    0
}

fn pin_display_dc() -> int64 {
    45
}

fn pin_display_clk() -> int64 {
    46
}

fn pin_display_mosi() -> int64 {
    3
}

fn pin_display_reset() -> int64 {
    1
}

fn display_reset_pulldown_ohms() -> int64 {
    100000
}

